 "findings": [
  {
   "id": "H-001",
   "severity": "High",
   "evidence_level": "analyzer_and_reasoning",
   "title": "Borrower blocks claim_default and collateral seizure by reassigning the owner of their USDC ATA",
   "component": "loan",
   "location": {
    "path": "src/instructions/escrow_instructions/loan.rs",
    "start": 773,
    "end": 780
   },
   "category": "ATA owner reassign",
   "category_key": "solana.ata_owner_reassign",
   "description": [
    {
     "p": "ClaimDefaultCtx requires recipient_loan_token to be the recipient's associated token account for the loan mint, typed with init_if_needed and associated_token::authority = recipient. The loan mint is classic SPL USDC (loan_token_program is Program<Token>). Classic SPL Token lets an account owner change the owner of an associated token account with SetAuthority AccountOwner; the account then still sits at the ATA address but its owner no longer matches, and Anchor's init_if_needed owner check rejects it."
    },
    {
     "p": "The recipient is the borrower, the party being liquidated. By reassigning their own USDC ATA they make every claim_default call fail. claim_default is the lender's seizure path, and the account is mandatory even when the surplus refund is zero. The same constraint exists in settle and sweep, but those only hurt the borrower."
    }
   ],
   "impact": [
    {
     "p": "A defaulting borrower keeps the principal and prevents the lender from seizing the collateral, removing the lender's whole recourse on the loan. The collateral stays frozen in the vault because claims are blocked while the loan is Active, which gives the borrower leverage to negotiate with the lender. The lender cannot undo this; only the borrower can restore the ATA owner."
    }
   ],
   "recommendation": [
    {
     "p": "Do not make the lender's seizure depend on a borrower-controlled account. Route any surplus refund in claim_default to the escrow's own loan ATA (left for sweep) or make recipient_loan_token optional and skip the surplus transfer when it is absent or its owner differs. Alternatively pay surplus to an account derived and owned by the program, so its owner cannot be reassigned."
    }
   ],
   "evidence": {
