  {
   "id": "M-001",
   "severity": "Medium",
   "evidence_level": "reasoning_challenged",
   "title": "Expired offer keeps the escrow in Offered and blocks the recipient's vesting claims",
   "component": "vesting_escrow",
   "location": {
    "path": "src/state/vesting_escrow.rs",
    "start": 236,
    "end": 242
   },
   "category": "Account relationship",
   "category_key": "solana.account_relationship",
   "description": [
    {
     "p": "enforce_claim allows claims on a loan lock only in Idle or Defaulted. publish_offer moves the escrow to Offered, and an offer that expires unfilled is not reset: fill rejects it, but the state remains Offered. The transition back to Idle exists only in withdraw_offer and in a new publish_offer, and both require the offer_authority signature."
    },
    {
     "p": "When offer_authority is a separate key (for example a service key chosen at open_lock), the recipient depends on that key to unlock vested tokens after any unfilled offer, and the authority can keep republishing to hold the escrow in Offered."
    }
   ],
   "impact": [
    {
     "p": "Vested collateral can be held unclaimable by the offer authority, or stays stuck if that key is lost, even though no loan is outstanding. A recipient using the default authority is not affected because the recipient can withdraw the offer."
    }
   ],
   "recommendation": [
    {
     "p": "Treat an expired Offered state as Idle in enforce_claim, or let anyone, or at least the recipient, call withdraw_offer once now is at or past offer_expiry."
    }
   ],
